<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.4.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00751</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.4.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>295fbde2-9043-40dd-8864-052104771fd8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<item>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> values for \(r\) that indicate a positive slope for the line of best fit.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>A: 1</item>
  <item>B: –1</item>
  <item>C: 0.5</item>
  <item>D: –0.5</item>
  <item>E: 0</item>
  <item>F: 0.8</item>
  <item>G: –0.8</item>
</list>  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1, 0.5, 0.8</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
<item>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> values for \(r\) that indicate a negative slope for the line of best fit.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>A: 0</item>
  <item>B: 1</item>
  <item>C: –1</item>
  <item>D: –0.87</item>
  <item>E: 0.32</item>
  <item>F: –0.24</item>
  <item>G: 0.24</item>
</list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –1, –0.87, –0.24</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
<item>The correlation coefficient, \(r\), is given for several different linear models. Order the correlation coefficients as follows: start with the \(r\)-value indicating the strongest linear relationship and end with the \(r\)-value indicating the weakest linear relationship.</item>
</list>
<para>0.4, –0.85, 0.72, –0.31</para>
<list>
<item> 0.72, 0.4, -0.31, –0.85</item>
    <item>–0.85, -0.31, 0.4, 0.72</item>
    <item>-0.31, 0.4, 0.72, –0.85, 0.72 </item>
    <item>–0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
<item>The correlation coefficient, \(r\), is given for several different linear models. Order the correlation coefficients as follows: start with the \(r\)-value indicating the strongest linear relationship and end with the \(r\)-value indicating the weakest linear relationship</item>
</list>
<para> –0.65, 0.47, –1, 0.89</para>
<list>
<item>–1, 0.89, –0.65, 0.47</item>
    <item>0.47, -0.65, 0.89, -1</item>
    <item> –1, –0.65, 0.47, 0.89  </item>
    <item>0.89, 0.47, –1, –0.65, -1</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>-1, 0.89, -0.65, 0.47</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
<item>Match the following scatter plots to the correct correlation coefficient from the following:</item>
</list>
<para>\(r=0.67\), \(r=-0.33\), \(r=0.88\), \(r= -0.79\)</para>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5c3073c9737f0a0cf23f4ceb082a4905b7924dd6"/></media></figure></para>

  <para>Scatter Plot A<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r=0.88\)</para>


  <para>Scatter Plot B<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r= -0.79\)</para>


  <para>Scatter Plot C<emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>:</emphasis> \(r= -0.33\)</para>


  <para>Scatter Plot D<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r=0.67\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
<item>Match each scatter plot with the correct correlation coefficient from the following:</item>
</list>
<para>\(r = 0.37\), \(r = 0.83\), \(r = -0.67\), \(r = -0.85\)</para>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6d07b8c04c7507ae55db4d8abb1a774e361644d5"/></media></figure></para>

  <para>Scatter Plot A<emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(r = -0.67\)</para>
  <para>Scatter Plot B<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r=0.83\)</para>
  <para>Scatter Plot C<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r = 0.37\)</para>
  <para>Scatter Plot D<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(r = -0.85\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
<item>Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe this scatter plot?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a3e5f256443b7065f434b4f2805fb6d9fdcf58d1"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item>–0.32</item>
  <item>0.87</item>
  <item>–0.87</item>
  <item>0.32</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –0.87</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
<item>Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe this scatter plot?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9a74b1315b2ca91f0badced5dc3cc085f8b912e1"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item>–0.62</item>
  <item>0.94</item>
  <item>–0.94</item>
  <item>0.62</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>: </emphasis>0.62</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
<item>Which of the following has the stronger linear relationship? Explain.</item>
</list>
<para>Scatter Plot A:</para>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/81ba1809d00f11bd8a2eed30d83f45a385d8823d"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Scatter Plot B:</para>
<para><figure><media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS A STRONG POSITIVE CORRELATION."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0e8567567754afd2ed200992508ac9e43957b2a0"/></media></figure></para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Scatter plot B because the points in the scatter plot are closer to forming a linear relationship. </para>
<para>10. Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe the scatter plot?</para>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/aca8f83947b57b52a355fc98e7c83b99e6545d17"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item>–0.89</item>
  <item>0.89</item>
  <item>0.43</item>
  <item>–0.43</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0.43</para>
 </section>
</content>
